 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Text: An invisible enemy\nPollution is the presence of harmful substances in the air, water or soil. In our cities, old vehicles and generators release thick smoke; factories pour waste water into rivers; plastic bags block gutters and choke animals; and loud music and horns cause noise pollution. The consequences are serious: coughs and asthma, diarrhoea and cholera from dirty water, fewer fish, poorer soils and stress. Pollution can be reduced: services can check vehicle exhaust, factories can treat their waste water, families can sort and recycle rubbish, and everybody can use fewer plastic bags. Pollution is an enemy we often do not see until it makes us ill.\n\nTypes of pollution: air, water, land (soil) and noise pollution.",
  "checks": []
 },
